# Without this file, `docker build`'s context (and every `COPY . .` in
# Dockerfile) includes the entire working directory as-is — node_modules
# with host-specific native bindings, a stale dist/ and tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
# that can make the builder stage's `nest build` silently skip re-emitting
# JS (tsc's incremental cache treating the copied-in .tsbuildinfo as
# up-to-date), and potentially .env.local secrets. Found the hard way: a
# build produced an image with only .d.ts files and no .js in dist/,
# entirely because a host-side tsconfig.tsbuildinfo leaked into the image.

node_modules
dist
build
coverage
.nyc_output

*.tsbuildinfo

.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.production
.env.staging

.git
.gitignore

logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

.claude

test
docs
k8s
*.md
